{
 "comment": "Scenarios of tests/abi/intersection_observation.py and its Chromium oracle intersection_observation_browser.mjs, in a 320x240 viewport. Steps run in order. update is one rendering update (Chromium: an animation frame and a task; native: rv_host_update) and closes a segment; deliveries are compared per observer within a segment, because the order between observers is the engine's (qualifiedScenarios record it). create takes IntersectionObserverInit with root null, '#document' or an element id, and logs a status. take is a synchronous takeRecords(); pair arms two observers so that the first to deliver takes the other's records. Times are checked against performance.now() (native: rv_host_now) around each update, never compared.",
 "markup": "<!doctype html><html><head><style>html,body{margin:0}body{width:600px;height:2000px;position:relative}#far{position:absolute;left:10px;top:400px;width:50px;height:50px}#s{position:absolute;left:100px;top:20px;width:200px;height:100px;overflow:auto}#sp{height:500px;position:relative}#u{position:absolute;left:10px;top:150px;width:50px;height:50px}#x{position:absolute;left:10px;top:150px;width:50px;height:50px}#c{position:absolute;left:10px;top:10px;width:80px;height:100px;overflow:hidden}#cp{height:300px;position:relative}#v{position:absolute;left:0;top:110px;width:50px;height:50px}</style></head><body><div id=far></div><div id=s><div id=sp><div id=u></div></div></div><div id=x></div><div id=c><div id=cp><div id=v></div></div></div></body></html>",
